:: Boardwalk Explore Tourist Photo [nobr]

/* Written by: Winters */
/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 20>>
The boardwalk hums with the sound of shouts and squeals of delights from the crowd, intermixed with the thrum of footsteps, and the steady crashing of ocean waves. Filling the air, along with the plethora of sounds, <span style="color:LightGreen">is the scent of hot caramel corn, deep-fried dough, and other delicious foods.</span> Navigating through the crowd, you slowly make your way down the boardwalk. To your right, various shops and arcades flash their signs and advertisements competing for your attention. <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Everyday",
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

Doing your best to ignore all of this, you continue to wander past the crowd when a voice calls out to you, breaking your stride. <br>
<br>

<<set _random to random(1, 2)>>

<<if _random == 1>>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Excuse me! Sorry, could you do us a huge favor?"</span> <br>
    <br>
    You blink and turn to find a woman in an oversized sunhat beaming at you. She is clutching a camera in her hands. Behind her, her family is already assembling themselves against the railing with the shimmering blue expanse of the ocean behind them. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Could you take a quick photo of us?"</span> <span style="color:Yellow">she asks, offering the camera with a hopeful smile.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <div id="choice">
        <<link "Agree<br>">>
        <<replace "#choice">>
            The woman beams down at you as you agree to take the picture. She quickly hands you over the camera, instructing you how to take the picture, before hurrying over to her family. <br>
            <br>
            You step back, lifting the camera to eye level to frame the shot. You tell everyone to get ready as you focus the camera. <br>
            <br>
            That's when you see him. <br>
            <br>
            Standing on the right side of the frame, leaning lightly against the wooden railing, is a boy who looks your age. <span style="color:Pink">He’s wearing a pair of faded red swim trunks, his bare shoulders lightly dusted with freckles and a faint sheen of saltwater. But it’s his face that catches you completely off guard. <br>
            <br>
            As you hold the camera up, he catches your eye through the screen and flashes a bright, unforced smile. It’s a genuinely cute smile, the kind that makes his eyes crinkle at the corners, and dimples show up just above his jawline. For a second, the bustling noise of the boardwalk fades into a quiet blur. Your heart does a strange, sudden flip in your chest.</span> You find yourself staring at his smile on the screen, momentarily forgetting what you’re actually supposed to be doing. <br>
            <br>
            <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Is it working?"</span> the mother asks with a small note of concern, breaking the spell. You quickly respond that everything is fine, feeling a sudden warmth creep up your neck. <br>
            <br>
            You take a breath, center the frame, and tap the shutter button a few times. Click. Click. Click. <span style="color:Pink">Through it all, his eyes stay locked onto yours, his smile widening as he looks at you. For a moment, it feels like you’re taking a private picture shared between just the two of you.</span> <br>
            <br>
            Lowering the camera, the woman thanks you as she steps towards you. You hand the camera back to the mother, who thanks you once again. As the family begins to scatter, you steal one last glance. The boy in the red swim trunks looks back over his shoulder, his cute smile returning for just a brief, lingering second before he turns to follow his family down the steps toward the beach. <br>
            <br>
            You stand there for a moment, the boardwalk humming beneath your feet again, a sudden, bright warmth blooming in your chest that has nothing to do with the summer sun. <br>
            <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
            <<set $Arousal += 10>>
            <br>
            [[Continue|Boardwalk]]
        <</replace>>
        <</link>>
        <<link "Refuse<br>">>
        <<replace "#choice">>
            <span style="color:LightCoral">A sudden, sharp knot tightens in your stomach. Your chest feels tight, and the casual chatter of the boardwalk suddenly sounds deafeningly loud. The thought of stepping into their space, taking their device, and having four sets of eyes staring at you while you fumble with a camera lens makes your palms sweat.</span> Your throat goes completely dry, and it takes some effort to stammer out a refusal. <br>
            <br>
            The woman’s smile falters, her eyebrows knitting together in confusion. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh, it'll just take a second…"</span> <br>
            <br>
            Before she can say another word, you pivot on your heel. Not looking back to see the baffled expressions on their faces, you bolt away in a near-sprint. Your feet clack loudly on the wood of the boardwalk as you weave wildly through people and food stands. Soon enough, you’re far enough away that you think you’ve disappeared into the crowd. Slowing down your pace, you try to act casual now that you’re away from the woman. Your heart is still hammering against your ribs like a trapped bird. <br>
            <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
            <<addMoodlet "Stress" 2>>
            <br>
            [[Continue|Boardwalk]]
        <</replace>>
        <</link>>
    </div>
<<else>>
    The source of the voice quickly becomes clear as a man steps directly into your path. <br>
    <br>
    He’s wearing a white baseball cap, a bright floral short, cargo pants, and a heavy camera dangling from his neck. The word tourist practically blinks in neon lights above his head. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Excuse me,"</span> he says, offering a wide, hopeful smile. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Do you mind taking a quick picture for me?"</span> <br>
    <br>
    <div id="choice">
        <<link "Agree<br>">>
        <<replace "#choice">>
            You shrug, offering a polite nod. You reach out, expecting him to hand over the heavy camera. Instead, he steps back, gesturing toward the railing where the beach stretches out behind him. <br>
            <br>
            <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh, actually, I want you in the picture with me,"</span> he says brightly. <br>
            <br>
            You blink, your hand dropping to your sides. <span style="color:Yellow">A knot of confusion tightens in your chest.</span> <br>
            <br> 
            The man lets out a booming laugh, as if you’ve just made a witty joke. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I know, I know! But I’m collecting memories from this trip, and I really want a picture with a local. You look like you live around here.”</span> He says as you as he looks you up and down. <br>
            <br>
            <span style="color:Yellow">You shift your weight from one foot to the other. It feels weird, but you don't want to make a scene or be rude. He’s just an overenthusiastic vacationer, right?</span> After a moment of consideration, you reluctantly step into the frame next to him. <br>
            <br>
            Before you can mentally prepare or even decide how to pose, the man extends his arm, reversing the camera to face the two of you. In the same breath, he throws a heavy, fleshy arm around your side. He pulls you in tight, forcing your other side to be flush against his. You can smell his sunscreen, sharp and chemical, mixed with the faint scent of sweat. <br>
            <br>
            Your entire body goes rigid. You freeze, a forced, bewildered half-smile plastered on your face as you stare blindly into the glass lens. <span style="color:LightCoral">Right before he takes the picture, the arm on your sides lowers to your backside, where he gives your butt cheek a firm squeeze. A small gasp escapes you.</span> <br>
            <br>
            Click. <br>
            <br>
            <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Perfect! Outstanding,"</span> the man beams, slowly releasing you from his grip. The sudden return of personal space makes you feel slightly dizzy. He looks down at the camera screen, nodding with deep satisfaction, completely oblivious to your stiff posture. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Thanks a lot, kid. Enjoy your day!"</span> <br>
            <br>
            With a cheerful wave, he turns and melts back into the bustling crowd, his floral shirt disappearing past the ice cream parlor. <br>
            <br>
            You stand frozen by the railing for a long moment, the ocean breeze suddenly feeling a little colder against your neck. You look at the space where he just was, then down at your feet. <span style="color:LightCoral">Your butt is throbbing slightly from the aggressive squeeze. The boardwalk hums around you, loud and indifferent, leaving you marooned in a quiet wave of confusion.</spaN> <br>
            <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
            <<addMoodlet "Stress" 2>>
            <br>
            [[Continue|Boardwalk]]
        <</replace>>
        <</link>>
        <<link "Refuse<br>">>
        <<replace "#choice">>
            Suddenly, the warmth of the afternoon vanishes. A cold knot tightens in your stomach. It’s not an unreasonable request, tourists ask for photos all the time, but everything inside you is screaming no. He’s standing too close. His posture feels predatory, cloaked in casual vacation wear. <span style="color:LightCoral">You can smell the sharp, metallic tang of his sweat mixed with cheap sunscreen, and it makes you want to gag.</span> <br>
            <br>
            Your heart thumps against your ribs. Every instinct you have tells you that being near this man, even for the a few seconds it takes to snap a photo, is a terrible idea. <br>
            <br>
            Your refusal comes out a bit sharper than you intended, cutting through the ambient noise of seagull cries and arcade music. <br>
            <br>
            The man’s smile falters, a flash of irritation darkening his features. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Come on, kid, it’ll take two seconds. Just a quick…"</span> <br>
            <br>
            Before he can finish or reach out, you sidestep him entirely. You don't look back to see his reaction. You just walk. Your pace quickens from a casual stroll to a near-power walk, your eyes locked dead ahead. You weave through a family pushing a stroller, slip past a group of teenagers laughing over ice cream, and lose yourself in the thick of the boardwalk crowd. <br>
            <br>
            Only when you are a safe distance away, surrounded by the comforting, noisy blur of strangers, do you finally let out the breath you didn't realize you were holding. <br>
            <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
            <<addMoodlet "Stress" 2>>
            <br>
            [[Continue|Boardwalk]]
        <</replace>>
        <</link>>
    </div>
<</if>>